1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,516
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,518 --> 00:00:02,938
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:02,944 --> 00:00:04,493
(Haemyeong University Hospital)

4
00:00:04,495 --> 00:00:06,108
(Episode 17)

5
00:00:08,585 --> 00:00:09,784
It's okay.

6
00:00:10,591 --> 00:00:14,300
O Reum, you have to get your shot
before we go to the pool.

7
00:00:14,468 --> 00:00:15,598
No.

8
00:00:15,755 --> 00:00:17,668
I don't want a shot.

9
00:00:18,612 --> 00:00:20,018
Could you give us a minute?

10
00:00:27,805 --> 00:00:29,723
I don't want to lie down.

11
00:00:31,650 --> 00:00:32,902
What should we do?

12
00:00:33,208 --> 00:00:36,632
I want to go home, to Grandma's house.

13
00:00:36,645 --> 00:00:37,674
O Reum,

14
00:00:37,842 --> 00:00:39,721
you said you wanted to go to the pool.

15
00:00:39,769 --> 00:00:41,379
You said you'd go swimming
with your uncle.

16
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:43,530
I'm not going. I don't want a shot.

17
00:00:43,532 --> 00:00:44,628
O Reum,

18
00:00:44,735 --> 00:00:48,270
don't you want to fly with me
to see Grandfather?

19
00:00:48,272 --> 00:00:50,658
Grandfather can come here.

20
00:00:51,272 --> 00:00:52,805
You can't even go to daycare.

21
00:00:52,871 --> 00:00:56,912
I said no. I want to go home.

22
00:00:59,832 --> 00:01:03,029
We've been monitoring
his response to chemotherapy,

23
00:01:03,111 --> 00:01:06,318
but due to a high-risk genetic
abnormality, his prognosis isn't good.

24
00:01:06,658 --> 00:01:07,806
Doctor,

25
00:01:08,363 --> 00:01:09,376
what should we do?

26
00:01:09,379 --> 00:01:12,497
I recommend
an allogeneic stem cell transplant.

27
00:01:12,498 --> 00:01:13,516
You...

28
00:01:14,644 --> 00:01:18,003
- mean a bone marrow transplant?
- Yes.

29
00:01:18,571 --> 00:01:22,876
You'll need to find a donor
whose HLA matches your child's.

30
00:01:22,878 --> 00:01:25,360
Hopefully, there's a match
within the family.

31
00:01:25,777 --> 00:01:29,437
If not, donors outside the family
are common these days too.

32
00:01:29,712 --> 00:01:30,982
Whoever it is,

33
00:01:31,837 --> 00:01:34,127
as long as the bone marrow matches,
that's all that matters, right?

34
00:01:34,402 --> 00:01:35,611
Yes, that's right.

35
00:01:41,498 --> 00:01:42,632
Did you draw here too?

36
00:02:04,932 --> 00:02:06,791
- What did she say?
- Where's Seung Woo?

37
00:02:06,912 --> 00:02:09,535
I told him to go buy something
for Mai to eat.

38
00:02:10,805 --> 00:02:11,816
Mom,

39
00:02:12,450 --> 00:02:13,478
we need to talk.

40
00:02:14,538 --> 00:02:15,928
Is it bad news?

41
00:02:15,931 --> 00:02:16,941
Wait a second.

42
00:02:16,995 --> 00:02:20,638
- I'll go ask O Reum's doctor for help.
- I'll tell her.

43
00:02:20,798 --> 00:02:22,358
Go in with her first.

44
00:02:23,532 --> 00:02:24,548
Okay, then.

45
00:02:25,196 --> 00:02:26,218
Mother.

46
00:02:27,088 --> 00:02:29,088
(Pediatric Vaccination)

47
00:03:59,885 --> 00:04:02,192
Of all things, this is all I have.

48
00:04:11,291 --> 00:04:12,904
The doctor recommended
a bone marrow transplant.

49
00:04:15,418 --> 00:04:17,401
How did things get this bad overnight?

50
00:04:17,542 --> 00:04:19,134
I can't believe this. Seriously!

51
00:04:20,112 --> 00:04:21,642
All those IV treatments he had,

52
00:04:22,005 --> 00:04:23,564
did they not work at all?

53
00:04:32,365 --> 00:04:34,042
You can't be like this, Seung Hyun.

54
00:04:36,118 --> 00:04:38,211
I keep having these terrible thoughts.

55
00:04:39,898 --> 00:04:41,198
No, don't.

56
00:04:41,898 --> 00:04:42,918
That can't happen.

57
00:04:43,512 --> 00:04:45,212
O Reum will get better. He has to.

58
00:04:49,112 --> 00:04:50,211
He will.

59
00:04:53,045 --> 00:04:55,767
So they need to check
for a bone marrow match?

60
00:04:56,765 --> 00:04:58,513
Siblings are more likely to be a match,

61
00:04:58,914 --> 00:05:01,233
but the chances aren't as high
between parents and children.

62
00:05:02,565 --> 00:05:04,111
We should still try.

63
00:05:04,198 --> 00:05:05,214
Yeah.

64
00:05:05,542 --> 00:05:07,628
If any of us is a match for O Reum,

65
00:05:07,956 --> 00:05:09,411
that would be the best news.

66
00:05:09,905 --> 00:05:10,998
I'll go first.

67
00:05:11,045 --> 00:05:13,611
Think of everyone who could be a match.
We have to get everyone tested.

68
00:05:13,778 --> 00:05:15,338
We don't know who will match.

69
00:05:16,672 --> 00:05:18,012
Don't do it.

70
00:05:18,792 --> 00:05:19,825
No,

71
00:05:20,505 --> 00:05:23,424
- do it later. Be the very last.
- Mother...

72
00:05:25,345 --> 00:05:26,365
He...

73
00:05:27,358 --> 00:05:30,398
Let's do it only
if there's really no one else.

74
00:05:32,932 --> 00:05:35,305
Why, Mom?

75
00:05:35,385 --> 00:05:39,108
That's right. If no one else is a match,
you can do it then.

76
00:05:40,169 --> 00:05:41,178
Yeah.

77
00:05:48,765 --> 00:05:50,458
You're different from everyone else.

78
00:05:50,707 --> 00:05:52,002
How am I different?

79
00:05:52,171 --> 00:05:53,900
Just because I lost a leg,
does that mean I have no bone marrow?

80
00:05:53,902 --> 00:05:55,738
- Seung Woo!
- Mom, seriously...

81
00:05:57,525 --> 00:05:58,925
You're making me feel miserable.

82
00:06:01,118 --> 00:06:02,678
Say whatever you want.

83
00:06:03,138 --> 00:06:04,228
That's how I feel.

84
00:06:04,985 --> 00:06:06,850
I just want you to do nothing.

85
00:06:07,419 --> 00:06:08,451
You...

86
00:06:09,878 --> 00:06:11,911
Don't let them take anything else
from your body.

87
00:06:17,838 --> 00:06:21,070
Yeong Ju, I'm really fine.

88
00:06:21,072 --> 00:06:23,210
If O Reum is sick,
how can I just do nothing?

89
00:06:23,212 --> 00:06:25,611
I should be the first to step up, right?

90
00:06:25,832 --> 00:06:28,411
You say Seung Hyun
is like a husband to you,

91
00:06:29,045 --> 00:06:30,049
but to me,

92
00:06:30,091 --> 00:06:32,831
he's like a father.

93
00:06:33,512 --> 00:06:36,405
If Seung Hyun ever needed it,
I'd even donate my liver, no,

94
00:06:36,685 --> 00:06:38,232
I'd give him my heart.

95
00:06:38,885 --> 00:06:39,894
Still,

96
00:06:40,042 --> 00:06:43,178
I don't want anyone
taking anything more from your body!

97
00:06:44,872 --> 00:06:46,405
Just stay out of it for now.

98
00:06:52,612 --> 00:06:54,254
That stubborn woman...

99
00:06:54,412 --> 00:06:55,698
There she goes again.

100
00:06:59,998 --> 00:07:01,618
Dad.

101
00:07:02,918 --> 00:07:07,366
Dad, we have to find a bone marrow match
for O Reum.

102
00:07:07,665 --> 00:07:09,490
You and mom should both get tested.

103
00:07:09,492 --> 00:07:13,522
And ask all the relatives too.
Tell them it's my request.

104
00:07:14,972 --> 00:07:17,898
If that doesn't work, bring everyone here.

105
00:07:21,232 --> 00:07:22,258
Dad.

106
00:07:23,791 --> 00:07:25,704
I'm sorry.

107
00:07:28,105 --> 00:07:29,245
I'm...

108
00:07:31,291 --> 00:07:33,711
I'm the worst daughter, right?

109
00:07:36,418 --> 00:07:37,445
Thank you.

110
00:07:43,545 --> 00:07:44,598
Mai.

111
00:07:46,274 --> 00:07:48,095
Honey.

112
00:07:50,405 --> 00:07:53,116
We should've had another child
when we talked about it.

113
00:07:54,264 --> 00:07:56,738
They say siblings are the best match.

114
00:07:56,739 --> 00:07:57,892
Forget it.

115
00:07:58,798 --> 00:08:00,485
What's the point of saying that now?

116
00:08:01,958 --> 00:08:05,525
- Mom really upset you, didn't she?
- Yeah, she went too far.

117
00:08:06,212 --> 00:08:08,663
- I don't like her anymore.
- I'm sorry.

118
00:08:09,798 --> 00:08:11,107
In mom's eyes,

119
00:08:11,390 --> 00:08:13,105
Seung Woo has always been
a very fragile son.

120
00:08:13,705 --> 00:08:15,163
When he injured his leg,

121
00:08:15,916 --> 00:08:18,207
he nearly died several times.

122
00:08:18,412 --> 00:08:21,306
Dad never even came.
Mom handled it all alone.

123
00:08:22,892 --> 00:08:26,371
Grandpa helped with everything
because I was young back then.

124
00:08:27,312 --> 00:08:29,684
So you really resent your dad?

125
00:08:30,132 --> 00:08:31,905
Seung Woo convinced mom,

126
00:08:31,949 --> 00:08:33,804
and he says he'll get tested
as a bone marrow donor.

127
00:08:34,898 --> 00:08:36,606
But between the two of us,

128
00:08:37,049 --> 00:08:39,072
I hope one of us is a match for O Reum.

129
00:08:39,761 --> 00:08:41,125
I'd feel bad for your dad too.

130
00:08:41,126 --> 00:08:44,034
That would be the best outcome.

131
00:08:45,022 --> 00:08:48,300
Still, I think we should at least check.

132
00:08:48,388 --> 00:08:50,218
It's simple anyway.

133
00:08:50,838 --> 00:08:54,198
If neither of us is a match...

134
00:08:55,625 --> 00:08:57,233
Let's not think that far ahead.

135
00:09:11,938 --> 00:09:15,198
- O Reum, did you have fun?
- Yeah.

136
00:09:15,321 --> 00:09:18,609
- Dad, why were you crying earlier?
- Me?

137
00:09:19,245 --> 00:09:21,795
- I wasn't crying.
- You were, though.

138
00:09:22,327 --> 00:09:25,205
Why? Because of me?

139
00:09:25,705 --> 00:09:27,704
Let's rest a bit and then eat.

140
00:09:27,858 --> 00:09:29,891
Grandma, come over here.

141
00:09:29,978 --> 00:09:31,525
You want me to come over there?

142
00:09:34,964 --> 00:09:37,686
Mother, you said
you have a younger brother, right?

143
00:09:39,125 --> 00:09:41,019
Yeah, uncle Il Dong.

144
00:09:42,652 --> 00:09:45,030
He should get tested too, right?

145
00:09:45,585 --> 00:09:48,845
Every time he sees me,
he calls me an idiot and snaps at me.

146
00:09:51,218 --> 00:09:52,904
I already called him.

147
00:09:53,492 --> 00:09:54,496
He said he'll get tested.

148
00:09:55,177 --> 00:09:56,654
Seung Woo!

149
00:09:56,895 --> 00:09:58,315
That's reassuring.

150
00:09:59,184 --> 00:10:01,798
- He agreed to get tested?
- Of course.

151
00:10:02,005 --> 00:10:03,744
He didn't even hesitate.
He said he'd come right away.

152
00:10:05,052 --> 00:10:06,299
I'm grateful.

153
00:10:09,158 --> 00:10:10,165
Nervous?

154
00:10:10,167 --> 00:10:13,528
No. You said he's a good person.
You wouldn't stop talking about him.

155
00:10:13,530 --> 00:10:15,445
Still, be a little nervous.

156
00:10:15,518 --> 00:10:17,908
That way, I can properly escort you.

157
00:10:17,910 --> 00:10:19,004
What?

158
00:10:19,492 --> 00:10:21,070
- Ji Hu!
- Welcome.

159
00:10:21,901 --> 00:10:22,928
Welcome.

160
00:10:25,112 --> 00:10:27,822
So Ji Ni is really the woman
you told me about?

161
00:10:27,824 --> 00:10:29,830
Yes, I still can't believe it.

162
00:10:29,858 --> 00:10:32,838
- You know the General?
- The General?

163
00:10:32,878 --> 00:10:36,205
Tae O, don't call me that
in front of just anyone.

164
00:10:36,738 --> 00:10:38,791
I earned a few stars in the Navy.

165
00:10:39,292 --> 00:10:43,196
- What a small world.
- It really is. Have a seat.

166
00:10:43,328 --> 00:10:44,336
Okay.

167
00:10:56,026 --> 00:10:57,130
Say hello.

168
00:10:57,132 --> 00:10:59,503
This is Lieutenant No Il Dong,
my comrade and former subordinate.

169
00:10:59,505 --> 00:11:00,922
Here, he's my chief of staff.

170
00:11:03,475 --> 00:11:05,275
- Hello.
- Hello.

171
00:11:06,185 --> 00:11:08,999
- General, anything else?
- No.

172
00:11:09,017 --> 00:11:10,031
Okay.

173
00:11:14,792 --> 00:11:17,178
Uncle, here's the portfolio.

174
00:11:21,023 --> 00:11:23,318
- The artwork feels fresh.
- Right?

175
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:25,996
See? I knew you had an eye for art.

176
00:11:25,998 --> 00:11:27,793
It only looks good to me
because she helped me the other day.

177
00:11:27,794 --> 00:11:29,205
What do I know about art?

178
00:11:29,225 --> 00:11:32,538
And why are you calling me Uncle?
At work, I'm the CEO.

179
00:11:33,972 --> 00:11:34,991
Okay.

180
00:11:36,772 --> 00:11:39,311
I'm really interested in K-Montessori.

181
00:11:39,313 --> 00:11:42,618
I thought only I used K-Montessori.
You use that term too?

182
00:11:43,276 --> 00:11:44,532
Really?

183
00:11:46,445 --> 00:11:48,994
If you take the music out of animation,

184
00:11:48,996 --> 00:11:51,523
the visuals alone often fall flat.

185
00:11:51,525 --> 00:11:54,719
I want children who can't hear
to feel the story too,

186
00:11:54,825 --> 00:11:57,632
- so I want the art to carry it all.
- What genre?

187
00:11:57,792 --> 00:12:00,005
I'm very interested in Korean folktales.

188
00:12:00,072 --> 00:12:01,832
"The Tale of Sim Cheong"
and "The Tale of Chunhyang," for example.

189
00:12:01,965 --> 00:12:04,505
You must be more familiar
with the Brothers Grimm or Andersen.

190
00:12:05,132 --> 00:12:06,258
That's true.

191
00:12:06,932 --> 00:12:08,682
They seemed fine when I was a child,

192
00:12:08,802 --> 00:12:11,251
but the original tales were quite cruel.

193
00:12:11,252 --> 00:12:14,098
What makes our folktales different?

194
00:12:16,472 --> 00:12:18,474
Take "Beauty and the Beast," for example.

195
00:12:18,476 --> 00:12:21,920
The kind heroine meets a prince,

196
00:12:21,974 --> 00:12:23,959
and her life suddenly works out.

197
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:25,645
But ours are different...

198
00:12:27,085 --> 00:12:28,891
Take "The Old Man with a Lump."

199
00:12:29,352 --> 00:12:31,991
He may be unattractive, but he's talented.

200
00:12:32,812 --> 00:12:35,489
He's neither a prince nor born rich.

201
00:12:35,966 --> 00:12:40,317
People accept and value him
because of his entertaining stories.

202
00:12:40,318 --> 00:12:43,607
So the idea is to focus
on original Korean storytelling.

203
00:12:43,609 --> 00:12:45,503
Original Korean storytelling...

204
00:12:47,098 --> 00:12:48,748
Yes, that's right.

205
00:12:48,991 --> 00:12:52,436
That's why I want to leave fine art
and move into this field.

206
00:12:53,990 --> 00:12:55,005
You're in.

207
00:12:57,785 --> 00:13:00,543
Uncle, so are you going to invest?

208
00:13:00,545 --> 00:13:03,025
I'm investing
because you hired an excellent employee.

209
00:13:03,138 --> 00:13:05,430
- Make sure you do well.
- Yes, sir!

210
00:13:05,942 --> 00:13:06,985
Ji Ni.

211
00:13:09,012 --> 00:13:12,310
I've never seen "The Old Man with a Lump"
interpreted that way either.

212
00:13:12,312 --> 00:13:15,781
But Ji Ni,
you have both beauty and talent.

213
00:13:16,627 --> 00:13:18,005
You're jumping to conclusions again.

214
00:13:20,665 --> 00:13:23,428
Everyone has a shadow as big as they are.

215
00:13:24,132 --> 00:13:26,151
Why would I be any different?

216
00:13:28,025 --> 00:13:30,330
I can't believe the woman
Father met was you, Ji Ni.

217
00:13:30,332 --> 00:13:31,517
What a surprise.

218
00:13:32,958 --> 00:13:35,812
"Where, in What Form,
Shall We Meet Again?"

219
00:13:36,265 --> 00:13:37,778
That reminds me of a book title.

220
00:13:38,606 --> 00:13:39,787
Have you read it?

221
00:13:40,193 --> 00:13:41,231
No.

222
00:13:43,451 --> 00:13:46,081
I didn't read much through high school.

223
00:13:46,392 --> 00:13:48,959
It sounds like an excuse,
but I was busy practicing piano.

224
00:13:50,012 --> 00:13:52,035
I started reading more
after studying abroad and changing majors.

225
00:13:52,069 --> 00:13:54,503
I was wondering how you went
from playing piano to...

226
00:13:54,511 --> 00:13:56,499
I had wrist tendinitis.

227
00:13:57,025 --> 00:13:58,774
Rest was the best cure, but I couldn't.

228
00:14:00,071 --> 00:14:03,464
Then I failed the prelims
of a competition I had to pass,

229
00:14:03,469 --> 00:14:04,718
and I was devastated.

230
00:14:05,072 --> 00:14:08,416
When I went abroad,
I switched my major to arts management.

231
00:14:08,612 --> 00:14:10,006
I was also getting tired of playing piano.

232
00:14:12,062 --> 00:14:13,360
To be honest...

233
00:14:14,972 --> 00:14:16,125
Can I say something?

234
00:14:19,132 --> 00:14:20,132
Yes.

235
00:14:20,744 --> 00:14:22,092
Actually, when I was young,

236
00:14:22,141 --> 00:14:24,705
I wanted to become a soldier
like my father,

237
00:14:24,742 --> 00:14:25,872
but it didn't work out.

238
00:14:26,045 --> 00:14:28,316
So I practiced the piano a lot.

239
00:14:28,897 --> 00:14:30,092
Because my mom liked it.

240
00:14:30,278 --> 00:14:32,234
Not because you liked playing the piano?

241
00:14:33,269 --> 00:14:34,747
My mom liked it.

242
00:14:36,332 --> 00:14:37,494
You don't understand, right?

243
00:14:37,975 --> 00:14:39,618
No, I do.

244
00:14:40,185 --> 00:14:42,436
I did it because my dad liked it too.

245
00:14:56,285 --> 00:14:57,760
The weather is nice.

246
00:15:18,278 --> 00:15:20,485
Looks like you've gotten close
to Director Ji Hu.

247
00:15:20,946 --> 00:15:23,203
Yeah. A little?

248
00:15:23,444 --> 00:15:25,658
Are you okay with that?
You weren't fond of him before.

249
00:15:25,666 --> 00:15:26,993
He apologized.

250
00:15:27,185 --> 00:15:30,049
And it's not my place
to interfere with who he dates.

251
00:15:30,051 --> 00:15:31,733
As long as I don't see Do Do Hee,
it's fine.

252
00:15:32,212 --> 00:15:34,354
Didn't he mention that you beat her up?

253
00:15:34,739 --> 00:15:35,745
No.

254
00:15:36,152 --> 00:15:37,185
I don't think he knows.

255
00:15:37,852 --> 00:15:39,732
I guess she didn't tell him.

256
00:15:39,898 --> 00:15:42,358
She probably kept quiet
because she was embarrassed.

257
00:15:42,578 --> 00:15:44,470
Either way, I don't care.

258
00:15:44,902 --> 00:15:46,292
You're taking it pretty well.

259
00:15:46,652 --> 00:15:48,369
If I keep thinking about it,

260
00:15:48,423 --> 00:15:49,480
I'll only make things harder for myself.

261
00:15:49,521 --> 00:15:50,938
That's Na Ji Ni's philosophy of life.

262
00:15:51,133 --> 00:15:52,151
Yeah.

263
00:15:57,258 --> 00:15:58,617
Thank you.

264
00:16:05,252 --> 00:16:06,388
Can I get some cold water?

265
00:16:06,415 --> 00:16:07,472
Yeah.

266
00:16:07,474 --> 00:16:08,645
Me too.

267
00:16:08,672 --> 00:16:10,958
Get me some juice. My blood sugar's low.

268
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:11,992
Yes, Mother.

269
00:16:15,212 --> 00:16:16,278
Here.

270
00:16:18,705 --> 00:16:20,056
Mother wants juice.

271
00:16:21,772 --> 00:16:24,901
By the way, what made her shop so much?

272
00:16:27,169 --> 00:16:28,694
Retail therapy.

273
00:16:28,715 --> 00:16:29,725
"Therapy?"

274
00:16:29,765 --> 00:16:31,541
Because father started
a publishing company.

275
00:16:31,575 --> 00:16:32,761
I see.

276
00:16:32,788 --> 00:16:34,172
Is he the only one
allowed to do whatever he wants?

277
00:16:34,318 --> 00:16:36,151
I can do whatever I want too.

278
00:16:38,865 --> 00:16:41,038
Father wants blue crab soup for dinner.

279
00:16:41,212 --> 00:16:42,337
Hurry and get the groceries.

280
00:16:44,325 --> 00:16:46,365
What a devoted daughter-in-law.

281
00:16:46,852 --> 00:16:49,318
You like what we bought today, right?

282
00:16:49,675 --> 00:16:51,659
I don't even remember what I bought.

283
00:16:51,698 --> 00:16:53,838
I was just annoyed
and kept swiping my card.

284
00:16:54,812 --> 00:16:56,838
But you bought a lot of nice things.

285
00:16:57,392 --> 00:16:59,016
Take whatever you like.

286
00:16:59,124 --> 00:17:00,185
Really?

287
00:17:00,645 --> 00:17:02,258
You graduated from art school too,

288
00:17:03,925 --> 00:17:06,281
so why don't you work
at Joong Bin's company?

289
00:17:06,302 --> 00:17:07,565
Me?

290
00:17:07,745 --> 00:17:09,498
I'm preparing for my exhibition...

291
00:17:09,625 --> 00:17:12,278
Are you even having that exhibition?

292
00:17:12,658 --> 00:17:14,451
That girl who graduated
from Hanguk University...

293
00:17:14,707 --> 00:17:18,085
joined as an employee, and they love her.

294
00:17:18,632 --> 00:17:20,721
Joong Bin's excited.

295
00:17:20,829 --> 00:17:23,731
Really?
I wonder who it is from Hanguk University.

296
00:17:24,098 --> 00:17:26,190
You should join his publishing company...

297
00:17:26,525 --> 00:17:28,556
- and help ruin it.
- What?

298
00:17:28,558 --> 00:17:30,660
Your father will be back soon,

299
00:17:30,662 --> 00:17:32,364
but Joong Bin is buried in his books.

300
00:17:32,398 --> 00:17:34,971
How can Ji Hu face him?

301
00:17:35,152 --> 00:17:36,905
He'll be too ashamed.

302
00:17:38,192 --> 00:17:41,998
But Mother,
how exactly do you want it to fail?

303
00:17:42,225 --> 00:17:45,758
- Ma'am, I'll go buy some blue crabs.
- What? Why blue crabs?

304
00:17:45,785 --> 00:17:48,703
Father said earlier that he wanted
blue crab soup for dinner...

305
00:17:48,705 --> 00:17:49,787
Forget it.

306
00:17:50,158 --> 00:17:51,973
Tell him to just eat peppers
with soybean paste.

307
00:17:51,981 --> 00:17:53,252
What crabs?

308
00:17:53,752 --> 00:17:55,691
Does he get everything he wants
just by saying it?

309
00:17:55,798 --> 00:17:57,691
I do what I want at home.

310
00:17:58,035 --> 00:17:59,233
Clean this up.

311
00:17:59,285 --> 00:18:00,665
My head hurts.

312
00:18:02,552 --> 00:18:04,911
Would you like to get manual therapy
at a Korean medicine clinic?

313
00:18:04,972 --> 00:18:07,742
Or should I massage you like this?

314
00:18:10,965 --> 00:18:14,351
Must be nice
being born to live like a queen.

315
00:18:15,471 --> 00:18:19,465
If this is how I relieve stress,
I welcome stress anytime.

316
00:18:22,738 --> 00:18:25,483
This one is perfect for me.

317
00:18:27,412 --> 00:18:29,940
By the way, about dinner...

318
00:18:30,222 --> 00:18:32,362
Would it really be okay
to serve only peppers with soybean paste?

319
00:18:33,521 --> 00:18:34,889
I'm telling you,

320
00:18:34,891 --> 00:18:37,325
I was about to go buy some blue crabs,
but I gave up.

321
00:18:37,472 --> 00:18:39,246
She got mad, asking if everything
has to go his way,

322
00:18:39,248 --> 00:18:41,132
and I thought we'd have a war today.

323
00:18:41,652 --> 00:18:44,998
It's such a relief the general
has a dinner appointment.

324
00:18:45,258 --> 00:18:47,621
Peace at last.

325
00:18:48,049 --> 00:18:49,512
Mrs. Kim really went too far.

326
00:18:49,607 --> 00:18:50,765
She could've been
a little more understanding.

327
00:18:50,785 --> 00:18:53,778
She even went on a shopping spree.
It kind of made me jealous.

328
00:18:54,498 --> 00:18:56,585
You've got a lot to be jealous of.

329
00:18:56,934 --> 00:18:59,267
Let me have a bite.
You're really enjoying that.

330
00:19:03,285 --> 00:19:04,736
You heard from Seung Woo, right?

331
00:19:06,531 --> 00:19:08,645
I feel so bad for them.

332
00:19:08,838 --> 00:19:10,899
Seung Hyun deserves some good luck.

333
00:19:11,005 --> 00:19:12,092
He's such a good guy.

334
00:19:29,571 --> 00:19:31,644
Did it hurt when you got the shot?

335
00:19:34,159 --> 00:19:35,185
Do you like it?

336
00:19:35,191 --> 00:19:37,261
No more shots.

337
00:19:37,262 --> 00:19:38,345
That's right.

338
00:19:38,465 --> 00:19:41,843
So that you don't have to get more shots,

339
00:19:41,931 --> 00:19:44,688
Grandma, your dad, and I...

340
00:19:44,716 --> 00:19:46,206
are all getting the shots instead.

341
00:19:46,265 --> 00:19:48,393
Mom, isn't the drawing lady coming?

342
00:19:48,974 --> 00:19:51,415
Why? Do you miss her?

343
00:19:51,436 --> 00:19:53,512
Hurry.

344
00:20:07,352 --> 00:20:08,425
Hello?

345
00:20:08,479 --> 00:20:09,612
Ji Ni.

346
00:20:10,576 --> 00:20:11,612
Is that you, O Reum?

347
00:20:12,092 --> 00:20:13,585
How did you call me?

348
00:20:15,192 --> 00:20:17,067
O Reum found your number,

349
00:20:17,142 --> 00:20:20,163
so I called. Is that okay?

350
00:20:21,618 --> 00:20:22,668
Yes, that's fine.

351
00:20:23,075 --> 00:20:24,515
I'll put him on.

352
00:20:24,525 --> 00:20:26,711
Ji Ni, I ate a lot.

353
00:20:26,725 --> 00:20:28,721
I ate three spoonfuls.

354
00:20:28,782 --> 00:20:30,604
Let's draw together.

355
00:20:30,912 --> 00:20:32,960
Really? Three spoonfuls?

356
00:20:33,081 --> 00:20:34,496
That's a lot.

357
00:20:34,910 --> 00:20:36,369
I should praise you.

358
00:20:39,018 --> 00:20:41,300
Is your family getting shots?

359
00:20:41,981 --> 00:20:43,438
Okay.

360
00:20:43,952 --> 00:20:46,025
I'll come by later.

361
00:20:48,471 --> 00:20:51,492
Okay, I'll call you later.

362
00:20:55,585 --> 00:20:57,945
Knock before you come in,
even if it's your daughter's room.

363
00:20:58,105 --> 00:21:00,450
- Who were you just talking to?
- Jung A.

364
00:21:00,471 --> 00:21:02,624
Should I call her? Are you sure?

365
00:21:02,665 --> 00:21:03,994
What's wrong?

366
00:21:05,186 --> 00:21:07,418
It's O Reum, right? It is, isn't it?

367
00:21:08,592 --> 00:21:10,358
- Yeah.
- He called you, didn't he?

368
00:21:10,378 --> 00:21:11,678
Not like you would've called first.

369
00:21:11,812 --> 00:21:13,738
- Was it his mom?
- Mom, please.

370
00:21:13,740 --> 00:21:14,878
Shameless woman.

371
00:21:15,005 --> 00:21:17,203
She came trying to latch onto our family,

372
00:21:17,204 --> 00:21:19,665
and now she's calling my daughter
because her son is sick?

373
00:21:19,860 --> 00:21:22,106
What, does she want us to come help?

374
00:21:22,952 --> 00:21:25,258
He called just to tell me
he ate three spoonfuls.

375
00:21:25,472 --> 00:21:27,032
Don't you feel sorry
for that child at all?

376
00:21:27,178 --> 00:21:29,312
- You raised a kid too, Mom.
- Enough.

377
00:21:29,491 --> 00:21:30,885
Take off that pain patch before you talk.

378
00:21:30,952 --> 00:21:32,290
This is unbelievable.

379
00:21:32,292 --> 00:21:33,892
What are you to that family anyway?

380
00:21:33,958 --> 00:21:36,149
Just sit still and mind your own business.

381
00:21:36,272 --> 00:21:37,579
And don't answer their calls.

382
00:21:51,285 --> 00:21:55,112
The person you are calling is unavailable.
You will be connected to...

383
00:22:09,718 --> 00:22:11,838
I won't say this is karma.

384
00:22:12,318 --> 00:22:14,238
I've heard that more than
a hundred times myself.

385
00:22:14,252 --> 00:22:16,184
- You and I...
- Don't say we're different.

386
00:22:16,212 --> 00:22:17,363
How are we any different?

387
00:22:17,365 --> 00:22:20,585
Everyone wants to protect
the person they love.

388
00:22:20,792 --> 00:22:21,921
Anyway,

389
00:22:21,969 --> 00:22:24,392
I didn't come here to argue
about who's right or wrong.

390
00:22:24,453 --> 00:22:27,043
Don't tell my daughter
to come visit O Reum in the hospital.

391
00:22:27,045 --> 00:22:28,050
What are you talking about?

392
00:22:28,052 --> 00:22:29,812
He called again this morning.

393
00:22:30,338 --> 00:22:31,936
Going on about whether he ate or not.

394
00:22:32,124 --> 00:22:33,392
Why is that?

395
00:22:33,605 --> 00:22:35,318
Do you really need that much sympathy?

396
00:22:35,405 --> 00:22:37,409
You act as if you care so much
about boundaries,

397
00:22:37,683 --> 00:22:39,632
- so why didn't you block my husband?
- Yeong Ju.

398
00:22:39,692 --> 00:22:42,892
I don't understand how a daughter
like that came from a mother like you.

399
00:22:43,012 --> 00:22:44,168
At least,

400
00:22:44,429 --> 00:22:47,185
she was most concerned
about a critically ill child.

401
00:22:47,531 --> 00:22:50,582
When my daughter-in-law apologized,
she said that's between the adults.

402
00:22:51,043 --> 00:22:53,300
She said she'd just focus on O Reum.

403
00:22:53,410 --> 00:22:54,692
Aren't you worse than your own daughter?

404
00:22:54,785 --> 00:22:56,164
What else could I have done?

405
00:22:56,505 --> 00:22:58,385
You're the one who made me like this.

406
00:22:58,532 --> 00:23:01,322
I can be kind to the whole world,
but not to this family.

407
00:23:02,312 --> 00:23:05,158
You might think I turned out like this
on my own,

408
00:23:05,245 --> 00:23:07,731
but I think it's your stubbornness
that did it.

409
00:23:10,232 --> 00:23:13,314
Anyway, I've said everything
I came to say.

410
00:23:13,458 --> 00:23:14,850
Don't cross the line anymore.

411
00:23:14,852 --> 00:23:16,996
Ji Ni is naive and too kind.

412
00:23:16,997 --> 00:23:18,218
Don't take advantage of her.

413
00:23:18,431 --> 00:23:20,269
You begged me to save your shares,

414
00:23:20,470 --> 00:23:23,592
but now that I've signed them away,
are you done with me?

415
00:23:24,304 --> 00:23:27,157
Na Se Ri, don't live like that.

416
00:23:27,505 --> 00:23:30,309
You don't know
what could happen to you someday.

417
00:23:30,410 --> 00:23:32,038
Don't say such awful things.

418
00:23:32,572 --> 00:23:35,228
Those things you said to Ji Ni and me...

419
00:23:35,315 --> 00:23:37,658
I remember them so clearly,
it makes me shudder.

420
00:24:10,032 --> 00:24:11,703
Thank you, Mother.

421
00:24:11,918 --> 00:24:15,093
Did O Reum call Ji Ni?

422
00:24:16,909 --> 00:24:17,998
Don't let him.

423
00:24:18,392 --> 00:24:19,782
Her mother won't like it.

424
00:24:20,460 --> 00:24:21,695
Did she call?

425
00:24:21,743 --> 00:24:23,301
She came to our house.

426
00:24:24,538 --> 00:24:27,980
She said not to ask Ji Ni for pity.

427
00:24:28,454 --> 00:24:30,078
It's because of me.

428
00:24:30,212 --> 00:24:32,054
It isn't anyone's fault.

429
00:24:32,943 --> 00:24:36,144
Our families just aren't close.

430
00:24:40,493 --> 00:24:43,265
Here. The cake.

431
00:24:43,488 --> 00:24:45,399
You even brought a cake?

432
00:24:48,318 --> 00:24:50,244
Of course, we need cake.

433
00:24:50,338 --> 00:24:51,885
We're starting a business.

434
00:24:52,538 --> 00:24:53,802
Hurry and cut it.

435
00:24:58,363 --> 00:24:59,405
Clap.

436
00:25:03,998 --> 00:25:06,519
Boss, hire part-time help already.

437
00:25:06,540 --> 00:25:07,763
I'm busy too.

438
00:25:07,765 --> 00:25:08,945
Why are you going back on your word?

439
00:25:09,025 --> 00:25:10,157
You said you'd take over this place.

440
00:25:10,185 --> 00:25:11,734
I did? When?

441
00:25:11,982 --> 00:25:13,205
I heard that too.

442
00:25:13,475 --> 00:25:14,532
Well...

443
00:25:14,533 --> 00:25:17,134
Back then, I hadn't even joined
the Art and Culture Center,

444
00:25:17,172 --> 00:25:20,177
and my future looked hopeless.
I had to do something to survive.

445
00:25:20,562 --> 00:25:21,932
- That's all.
- Why?

446
00:25:22,038 --> 00:25:23,727
Are things different now?

447
00:25:23,818 --> 00:25:24,973
You think you're somebody now?

448
00:25:25,987 --> 00:25:27,146
Are you?

449
00:25:27,314 --> 00:25:29,101
Seriously, you people...

450
00:25:29,455 --> 00:25:31,965
Okay, I'll try it for now.

451
00:25:32,958 --> 00:25:34,445
I'll help you whenever I can.

452
00:25:34,592 --> 00:25:36,251
Isn't your publishing job paying enough?

453
00:25:36,253 --> 00:25:38,231
The more money you have, the better.

454
00:25:39,351 --> 00:25:40,771
That's the real world.

455
00:25:40,798 --> 00:25:43,831
You have one week
while the office is being redone.

456
00:25:43,892 --> 00:25:46,931
They'll use part of father's old room
to expand the office.

457
00:25:47,452 --> 00:25:50,358
I suggested starting
with just the two of you for now.

458
00:25:51,671 --> 00:25:52,718
Okay, that sounds good.

459
00:25:52,772 --> 00:25:54,579
Tae O and I will choose the items,

460
00:25:54,613 --> 00:25:56,561
and if we need more help,
I'll tell the CEO.

461
00:25:56,562 --> 00:25:57,570
Okay.

462
00:25:57,572 --> 00:25:59,761
You didn't get in, but you have a path.

463
00:25:59,842 --> 00:26:02,758
I got in, yet I feel stuck. Why?

464
00:26:02,865 --> 00:26:05,605
Jung A, focus more on your painting.

465
00:26:06,252 --> 00:26:08,745
The professors also speak highly
of your work.

466
00:26:09,165 --> 00:26:12,358
The Art and Culture Center
is planning a group exhibition.

467
00:26:13,511 --> 00:26:15,298
Things aren't looking bad right now.

468
00:26:15,512 --> 00:26:17,012
You'll do well from now on.

469
00:26:17,165 --> 00:26:19,551
Yes. I'm counting on you.

470
00:26:20,659 --> 00:26:24,211
Cheers.

471
00:26:30,605 --> 00:26:31,605
The baby?

472
00:26:31,828 --> 00:26:32,828
Yes.

473
00:26:32,900 --> 00:26:33,900
A baby?

474
00:26:35,785 --> 00:26:37,478
There's a sick baby.

475
00:26:37,985 --> 00:26:40,352
Ji Ni, follow your heart.

476
00:26:40,412 --> 00:26:41,571
Don't worry about your mom.

477
00:26:41,619 --> 00:26:44,101
Yes, I'm with you this time too.

478
00:26:44,268 --> 00:26:45,711
I feel sorry for the poor child.

479
00:27:10,298 --> 00:27:12,865
No one at all? That can't be.

480
00:27:12,932 --> 00:27:14,091
Am I not a match either?

481
00:27:14,272 --> 00:27:16,344
Even with the samples from Vietnam,

482
00:27:17,802 --> 00:27:19,521
none of them matched.

483
00:27:25,271 --> 00:27:26,598
Mom.

484
00:27:26,712 --> 00:27:28,387
We'll check...

485
00:27:28,748 --> 00:27:31,072
the overseas bone marrow donor registry.

486
00:27:32,065 --> 00:27:33,651
There is still one more person.

487
00:27:36,212 --> 00:27:37,875
There is one more person.

488
00:27:47,678 --> 00:27:49,104
What did you want to draw again?

489
00:27:49,105 --> 00:27:52,532
- A rainbow.
- Shall we draw a rainbow?

490
00:27:55,912 --> 00:28:01,505
- One, two, three.
- Whoosh.

491
00:28:20,401 --> 00:28:23,421
(Family Register)

492
00:28:23,438 --> 00:28:25,472
Why let your pride get in the way?

493
00:28:25,485 --> 00:28:27,829
You and your mother are both way too much.

494
00:28:27,831 --> 00:28:30,632
- Do I look selfish to you?
- Who says that?

495
00:28:30,634 --> 00:28:33,699
How much can you forgive
when someone you love has lied?

496
00:28:33,705 --> 00:28:35,505
I think the whole thing is a lie.

497
00:28:35,507 --> 00:28:37,270
Can you get tested just once?

498
00:28:37,271 --> 00:28:38,856
Get out. I said get out!

499
00:28:38,858 --> 00:28:40,470
I know this breaks your heart,

500
00:28:40,471 --> 00:28:42,492
but this still isn't right.

501
00:28:43,776 --> 00:28:45,776
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
